<speak>It sounds as though you've already got a useful example at home. You can adapt it rather than start from scratch. With the renovation papers, it may also help to keep a short list of outstanding administrative questions at the front, so they don't get scattered across email, handwritten notes and messages. That list is for your own household use, of course. If something requires professional guidance from the contractor or building management, it's best directed to them rather than guessed from an old email.</speak>